      "direction": "ltr",
      "text": "Rabbi Nechunia ben Hakana said, \"One verse states, <i>'And now men see not the light which is bright in the skies,'</i> (Job 37:21). Another verse states, <i>'He made darkness His hiding-place'</i> (Psalms 18:12). And it says, <i>'Clouds and darkness surround Him'</i> (Psalms 97:2). This is a difficulty. A third scripture reconciles them: <i>'Even the darkness is not too dark for You, But the night shines as the day; the darkness is as the light'</i> (Psalms 139:12).\""
    }
